SPOILERS

According to the spoilers being chaotic and sacrificing a human on a
chaotic altar increases your luck +2. Not seeing four leaf clovers
doesn't necessarily mean your luck hasn't increased (reconciliation,
gems at unicorns, etc).

The problem with sacrificing on level 1 is because the monsters are too
weak. You can convert an altar with ANY monster, but goblins, jackals,
newts, various molds, and all the other usual monsters you find on the
first few levels do nothing for your luck. You can tell because you get
the "consumed in a burst of flame" message but not the "four leaf
clover" message.

The solution:
	      Run through the dungeon to level 4 or 5 without fighting
anything you can avoid, then work your way back up. By the time you get
back to level 1, you should be a much higher level character. Hang
around there, and the monsters being created should be now big enough to
sacrifice successfully. Any that aren't provide you with food so you can
hang around sacrificing even longer.

